text:
It is not summer yet, but there’s a day-long sun;
There are no leaves on any tree as I pass by:
The wind has died; it does not blow its way through me;
I am without warmth, and I do not know why.

Oh, spring! you have come before your time away.
Why did you go to that fair city where they say
The grass will always be greener? The flowers never die;
They cannot love, or change their mind when tired.

Spring, we were born too soon this year--too young
